Additional native rule-pack attribution

The optional `rustleaks-providers-v1` rules and the database URI rule in
`rustleaks-connections-v1` are adapted from Betterleaks
commit `8f376ff9c31ed5309ac448fe601c5dd21b376155`:
https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks

Rustleaks changes rule identifiers, descriptions, ASCII case and whitespace
notation, and configuration fields. Incremental companion rules select only
reviewed new formats or delimiters. It uses its own source and finding policy;
provider validation is not included. The source revision, original patterns,
transformations and hashes are recorded in
`crates/rustleaks-core/default/rustleaks-providers-v1.provenance.json` (under
`default/` in the core package) and the adjacent
`rustleaks-connections-v1.provenance.json`. The URI adaptation restricts
schemes and bytes to its documented ASCII database dialect, retains all
relevant rejection predicates, and omits confidence computations and live
validation. These adapted rules retain the following
