The optional `rustleaks-connections-v1` rules adapt the five first-party
Kingfisher definitions at commit
`01e7b817376fbf2272be8f162bd32309bf97ee1f`.

Copyright 2025-2026 MongoDB, Inc.
https://www.mongodb.com

Source repository: https://github.com/mongodb/kingfisher

These rule assets retain the Apache License, Version 2.0; its exact text is
included in the adjacent `LICENSE.kingfisher`. Rustleaks changes identifiers,
descriptions, regex notation and ASCII scope, maps all source substring
exclusions to secret stopwords, and unrolls the bounded JDBC option repetition.
Original patterns, transformations and source hashes are recorded in the
adjacent `rustleaks-connections-v1.provenance.json`. This pack includes no
Kingfisher scanner implementation. The separately attributed URI rule above
is derived from Betterleaks; its provenance records the reviewed Kingfisher
overlay and its inapplicability to database schemes.

The optional `rustleaks-providers-v1` pack also adapts fifteen Veles
(OSV-SCALIBR) credential expressions from commit
`e8621f1fff93beb5b70e5d6ba5fdc3e9854ec845`:
https://github.com/google/osv-scalibr

Copyright 2026 Google LLC
Copyright 2025 Google LLC (additional xAI source header)

These expressions retain the Apache License, Version 2.0, whose exact source
text is included in the adjacent `LICENSE.veles`. The pinned archive records
no upstream NOTICE. Rustleaks changes identifiers and descriptions, wraps the
complete token in capture 1, and uses its existing source and finding policy.
No network validators or scanner implementation are included. The adjacent
`rustleaks-providers-v1.provenance.json` records individual source paths,
pattern lines, hashes, finite lengths and the xAI source-selection decision.

The optional `rustleaks-connections-v1` pack also adapts conservative Git
credential URL subsets from the same pinned Apache-2.0 Veles source. The
Bitbucket, CodeCatalyst and CodeCommit detector and Git-basic-auth helper
sources retain Copyright 2026 Google LLC. Rustleaks uses bounded unescaped
ASCII subsets that preserve the reviewed source URL-parser predicates,
case-sensitive path suffixes and complete URL capture. The exact source URLs,
hashes and modifications are recorded in the connection provenance JSON;
the source license remains in `LICENSE.veles`. No validator code is imported.
The native ADC refresh-token selection captures only the credential value,
with its independent bounds and issuer context recorded in provider provenance.

The provider pack's additional Betterleaks and Veles format selections retain
all applicable source filters and the recorded generated supersession filters.
Rustleaks narrows alphabets and boundaries to the documented ASCII selections.
The HCP and Packagist selections retain secret-only detection without importing
validation-only components. HCP, Packagist and Slack refresh retain original
fixed-width prefix extraction. Complete versioned GitLab PAT and Monday JWT
extraction may overlap retained findings. Original source expressions, exact
file hashes, license identities and modifications are recorded in the same
provider provenance JSON. The adjacent source license texts remain unchanged.

The provider and connection packs also adapt selected Azure, MongoDB, service
URI, JWT and Kubernetes detection contracts from the pinned MIT Betterleaks
configuration. The Cloudflare provider expression derives from the pinned
Apache-2.0 Veles detector. Adjacent provenance records immutable source URLs,
digests, original detection fields, tuple-predicate adaptations and explicit
scope restrictions. Existing LICENSE.betterleaks and LICENSE.veles cover these
sources; no validator or revoker implementation is included.

The provider pack additionally adapts twenty-six associated credential rules
and thirty hidden support rules from pinned Betterleaks generated definitions.
The AWS session-token definition is a Kingfisher overlay at commit
`01e7b817376fbf2272be8f162bd32309bf97ee1f`, under the adjacent
`LICENSE.kingfisher` Apache-2.0 text. Other association expressions retain the
adjacent `LICENSE.betterleaks` MIT attribution. Rustleaks preserves required
edges, local predicates and source byte-entropy decisions through its native
buffer-local contract. Explicit bytes-v1 patterns retain the generated source
expressions, raw byte bridges, inline flags and delimiter ranges. Provider
provenance records each generated pattern hash and source-selection decision.

Two additional Packagist roles adapt the pinned Apache-2.0 Veles detector
expressions at commit `e8621f1fff93beb5b70e5d6ba5fdc3e9854ec845`.
Copyright 2026 Google LLC. The exact license remains in `LICENSE.veles`.
Rustleaks adds token boundaries and selects independent reporting ACS and ACK
roles using the recorded source and issuer evidence. It imports no tuple
selection, online validation or revocation implementation. Exact source URLs,
line numbers, hashes and semantic selections remain in provider provenance.

The Mapbox secret-token and Vercel AI Gateway definitions additionally adapt
Betterleaks commit `8f376ff9c31ed5309ac448fe601c5dd21b376155` under the adjacent
`LICENSE.betterleaks` MIT terms, as generated by Kingfisher commit
`01e7b817376fbf2272be8f162bd32309bf97ee1f`. Their exact source byte patterns,
distinct global filter/prefilter fields and local predicates are recorded in
provider provenance. The Vercel predicate's pinned cl100k data and algorithm
attribution are maintained with its native predicate asset and MIT notices.

The Bitwarden CLI client-secret rule adapts Google OSV-SCALIBR Veles commit
`e8621f1fff93beb5b70e5d6ba5fdc3e9854ec845`, copyright 2026 Google LLC, under
the adjacent `LICENSE.veles` Apache-2.0 terms. The original property grammar,
literal path suffix, source hashes and direct-property selection are recorded
in provider provenance. No online validator, analysis or revocation code is
imported by these rules.
